  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What is an electric fuse? Explain its functions briefly. (3 marks)', 'An electric fuse is a safety device consisting of a short, thin wire made of a material with a low melting point (such as a tin-lead alloy), placed in a holder and connected in series with the live wire of a circuit or appliance.
It works on the heating effect of electric current. When the current rises above the safe value - because of a short circuit, an overload or a fault - the fuse wire heats up and melts, breaking the circuit and stopping the current.
Functions: it protects the wiring and appliances from damage due to excess current and prevents electrical fires and shocks. Each fuse has a rating slightly above the normal working current of the circuit (e.g. 5 A for lighting, 15 A for power); after a fault it must be replaced. Modern installations often use miniature circuit breakers (MCBs), which can be reset.', null, '[{"point": "A safety device: a short piece of thin wire of low melting point (tin-lead alloy) connected in series with the circuit/appliance (live wire)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Works on the heating effect of current: when current exceeds the rated value (short circuit or overload), the wire heats and melts, breaking the circuit", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Function: protects wiring and appliances from damage and prevents fires; rating chosen slightly above normal current (e.g. 5 A, 15 A); MCBs now often used instead", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
