  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What is a balanced diet? (3 marks)', 'A balanced diet is one that provides all the nutrients the body needs - carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, water and dietary fibre - in the correct proportions and amounts to meet the person''s energy and nutritional requirements.
The amount needed varies with age, sex, body size, physical activity and conditions such as pregnancy, breastfeeding or illness. A balanced diet maintains good health, normal growth and a healthy body weight and protects against both under-nutrition and non-communicable diseases.
In practice it means: cereals such as rice, maize or buckwheat for energy; pulses, meat, fish, eggs and dairy for protein; plenty of vegetables and fruits for vitamins, minerals and fibre; small amounts of fats and oils; and limiting salt, sugar and fatty foods (e.g. salty butter tea and very cheesy dishes).', null, '[{"point": "A diet that contains all nutrients - carbohydrates, proteins, fats, vitamins, minerals, water and fibre - in the right proportions/amounts", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Meets the energy and nutrient needs of the individual according to age, sex, activity, pregnancy/illness, maintaining health and normal weight", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Examples/guidance: cereals (rice/maize) for energy, pulses/meat/eggs/dairy for protein, vegetables and fruits for vitamins and minerals, limited fat, salt and sugar (e.g. avoid excess salt/butter tea, chilli-cheese)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
