  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What is the meaning of amalgamation with reference to chemistry? Give examples. (3 marks)', 'In chemistry, amalgamation is the process of forming an amalgam - an alloy of mercury with another metal. Mercury dissolves many metals such as gold, silver, tin, zinc and sodium.
Examples: dental amalgam (mercury with silver, tin and copper) used to fill teeth; sodium amalgam, used as a reducing agent in the laboratory; gold and silver amalgams.
In metallurgy, amalgamation is used to extract gold and silver from crushed ores: the precious metal dissolves in mercury, and the amalgam is then heated so that the mercury evaporates, leaving the metal. Because mercury vapour is toxic, this method causes health and environmental hazards.', null, '[{"point": "Amalgamation: formation of an alloy of mercury with another metal (an amalgam)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Examples: dental amalgam (mercury + silver, tin, copper) for tooth fillings; sodium amalgam (reducing agent); gold/silver amalgam", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Use in metallurgy: extraction of gold and silver from ores by amalgamation, then heating to drive off mercury (mercury is toxic - environmental concern)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
