  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'What is the chemical name of vitamin B1? Name the disease caused by its deficiency in human beings. (3 marks)', 'The chemical name of vitamin B1 is thiamine (thiamin). It acts as a coenzyme (thiamine pyrophosphate) in carbohydrate metabolism.
Its deficiency causes beriberi: dry beriberi affects the nerves (numbness, muscle weakness, difficulty walking), and wet beriberi affects the heart (breathlessness, swelling of the legs, heart failure). In heavy drinkers, deficiency causes Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome (confusion, memory loss).
Thiamine is found in whole grains, parboiled or unpolished rice, pulses, nuts and meat. Diets based on highly polished white rice, and alcoholism, lead to deficiency; outbreaks have occurred in boarding schools and monastic institutions in Bhutan, where thiamine supplements are now given.', null, '[{"point": "Vitamin B1 = thiamine (thiamin)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Deficiency disease: beriberi (dry - nerves/paralysis, wet - heart failure/oedema); also Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome in alcoholics", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Sources/prevention: whole grains, unpolished/parboiled rice, pulses, meat; deficiency linked to polished rice diets and alcohol (outbreaks reported in Bhutanese monastic schools)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
