  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'A wire of length L and resistance R is stretched so that its length is doubled. Explain how (i) its resistance and (ii) its resistivity change. (3 marks)', 'When the wire is stretched its volume stays the same (V = A × L). If the length doubles to 2L, the cross-sectional area must halve to A/2.
(i) Resistance: R = ρL/A. New resistance R'' = ρ(2L)/(A/2) = 4ρL/A = 4R. The resistance becomes four times the original.
(ii) Resistivity: ρ is a property of the material (and temperature) only, not of its length or thickness, so the resistivity does not change.', null, '[{"point": "Volume stays constant: doubling the length halves the cross-sectional area (A → A/2)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "(i) R = ρL/A → ρ(2L)/(A/2) = 4R: resistance becomes four times", "marks": 1}, {"point": "(ii) Resistivity is unchanged - it depends only on the material and temperature, not on dimensions", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
